1.23.3: the wipe says what it shows

The wipe had two faults of design, not placement. Its one dropdown
read "vs original" while the view could itself be the original, and
the page then swapped the comparison silently; and the other image
was clipped to its picture area, so outside it (a Polaroid's crop
ending before the original's edge) the view showed through, which
reads as a glitch.

Now one function composes the stage. The right of the divider is the
view - original, A or current, the buttons; the left is the image
chosen in a "left:" dropdown, shown whole, borders included, laid at
the input's pixel scale so the two pictures coincide and clipped only
to the view's box and the divider. Choosing for the left what is on
view moves the choice to its counterpart and the dropdown shows it. A
new render while the original is on view recomposes, since the
current may be the left side.

The Chromium test's 54-case placement check now also asserts the
dropdown names the image actually on the left.

